IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `coa-core`
IMPORT `coa21-ch3-squeeze-out`
IMPORT `coa21-ch3-sell-out`
IMPORT `coa-proc-takeover-notices`

-- coa-proc-takeover-notices-tests.l4: tests for coa-proc-takeover-notices.l4 (Companies Act 2006, ss 979 to 986).
-- Every expected outcome is written from the text of the section named beside it, before the run, and never copied from the output.
-- A #TRACE prints FULFILLED, a BREACH or a still-open obligation (RESIDUAL) and no assertion line, so the expected outcome sits on the
-- `-- EXPECT` line directly above each trace and is read against the Result block by expect_check.py.
-- Day 0 of each trace is the day named on the TIMELINE line of the rule, in calendar days.
-- Dates used: the offer is made on 1 January 2026 and can be accepted until 30 April 2026.
-- Six months beginning with 1 January end on 30 June (day 180 of the s 980(2) rule); three months beginning with 1 May end on 31 July (day 211).
-- A notice dated 1 February 2026 has its six weeks end on 15 March 2026 (28 days to 1 March, then 14).
-- The end of the acceptance period is 30 April 2026: one month on is 30 May (30 days); three months on is 30 July (91 days);
-- three months from a notice dated 30 May is 30 August (122 days).

§ `Tests for the takeover notices procedure`

§§ `Fixtures`

`an offer made on 1 January 2026, open until 30 April 2026, whose acceptance time is not governed by Schedule 1C rules` MEANS `ss 979-986 offer` OF (Date 1 1 2026), (Date 30 4 2026), FALSE
`an offer made on 1 January 2026, open until 30 April 2026, whose acceptance time is governed by Schedule 1C rules` MEANS `ss 979-986 offer` OF (Date 1 1 2026), (Date 30 4 2026), TRUE

-- the block fields, in order: class; value; voting rights; the date allotted or released after the offer (none); how the offeror stands to it; subsection (10) applies.
`ninety-five of a hundred acquired by acceptances` MEANS `s 979 block of shares` OF "ordinary", 95, 95, NOTHING, `s 979 acquired or unconditionally contracted to be acquired by virtue of acceptances of the offer`, FALSE
`five of a hundred not acquired` MEANS `s 979 block of shares` OF "ordinary", 5, 5, NOTHING, `s 979 not acquired or contracted to be acquired`, FALSE
`eighty-five of a hundred acquired by acceptances` MEANS `s 979 block of shares` OF "ordinary", 85, 85, NOTHING, `s 979 acquired or unconditionally contracted to be acquired by virtue of acceptances of the offer`, FALSE
`fifteen of a hundred not acquired` MEANS `s 979 block of shares` OF "ordinary", 15, 15, NOTHING, `s 979 not acquired or contracted to be acquired`, FALSE

-- the position fields, in order: the offer relates to shares of different classes; the blocks; the day the entitlement is determined; the holder's class;
-- the shares are voting shares; the holder's shares are ones the offeror has not acquired.
`an offeror with ninety-five per cent by acceptances and a holder who has not accepted` MEANS `ss 979-986 the offeror's position` OF FALSE, (LIST `ninety-five of a hundred acquired by acceptances`, `five of a hundred not acquired`), (Date 1 2 2026), "ordinary", TRUE, TRUE
`an offeror with eighty-five per cent by acceptances and a holder who has not accepted` MEANS `ss 979-986 the offeror's position` OF FALSE, (LIST `eighty-five of a hundred acquired by acceptances`, `fifteen of a hundred not acquired`), (Date 1 2 2026), "ordinary", TRUE, TRUE

-- the holdings fields, in order: value and voting rights of all the voting shares; acquired by acceptances (value, votes); other shares acquired (value, votes);
-- contracted subject to conditions (value, votes); an associate's shares acquired (value, votes); an associate's shares contracted subject to conditions (value, votes);
-- treasury shares (value).
`holdings that reach ninety-five per cent` MEANS `s 983 holdings` OF 100, 100, 95, 95, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0
`holdings that stop at eighty per cent` MEANS `s 983 holdings` OF 100, 100, 80, 80, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0

-- the answer of the existing s 983(2) function: an all-shares offer, a holder who has not accepted, some but not all acquired by acceptances, tested on 20 April 2026
-- (before the end of the acceptance period on 30 April 2026).
`a holder who may require the offeror to acquire the shares` MEANS `s 983(2) the holder of voting shares may require the offeror to acquire them` (`s 983(1) subsections (2) and (3) apply` TRUE) TRUE TRUE (Date 20 4 2026) (Date 30 4 2026) `holdings that reach ninety-five per cent` `holdings that reach ninety-five per cent`
`a holder who may not yet require the offeror to acquire the shares` MEANS `s 983(2) the holder of voting shares may require the offeror to acquire them` (`s 983(1) subsections (2) and (3) apply` TRUE) TRUE TRUE (Date 20 4 2026) (Date 30 4 2026) `holdings that stop at eighty per cent` `holdings that stop at eighty per cent`

§§ `Assertions: the Boolean helpers`

-- s 979(2): ninety-five per cent by acceptances entitles the offeror to give notice to a holder who has not accepted.
#ASSERT `ss 979-986 the offeror is entitled to give notice to the holder of the shares` (`an offeror with ninety-five per cent by acceptances and a holder who has not accepted`)
-- s 979(2)(a): eighty-five per cent is short of ninety.
#ASSERT (NOT (`ss 979-986 the offeror is entitled to give notice to the holder of the shares` (`an offeror with eighty-five per cent by acceptances and a holder who has not accepted`)))
-- s 980(2)(b) and (3): the offer is not governed by Schedule 1C rules, so the six months beginning with 1 January end on 30 June, earlier than the three months (31 July).
#ASSERT (`ss 979-986 the last day on which a notice may be given` (`an offer made on 1 January 2026, open until 30 April 2026, whose acceptance time is not governed by Schedule 1C rules`)) EQUALS (JUST (Date 30 6 2026))
-- s 980(2)(a): the offer is governed by Schedule 1C rules, so subsection (3) does not apply and the three months from 1 May end on 31 July.
#ASSERT (`ss 979-986 the last day on which a notice may be given` (`an offer made on 1 January 2026, open until 30 April 2026, whose acceptance time is governed by Schedule 1C rules`)) EQUALS (JUST (Date 31 7 2026))
-- s 980(2): a notice given on 30 June 2026 is in time.
#ASSERT `ss 979-986 section 979 allows a notice given on the day` (`an offer made on 1 January 2026, open until 30 April 2026, whose acceptance time is not governed by Schedule 1C rules`) (`an offeror with ninety-five per cent by acceptances and a holder who has not accepted`) (Date 30 6 2026)
-- s 980(2): a notice given on 1 July 2026 is after the end of the six months.
#ASSERT (NOT (`ss 979-986 section 979 allows a notice given on the day` (`an offer made on 1 January 2026, open until 30 April 2026, whose acceptance time is not governed by Schedule 1C rules`) (`an offeror with ninety-five per cent by acceptances and a holder who has not accepted`) (Date 1 7 2026)))
-- s 979(2): a notice given in time by an offeror short of ninety per cent is not a notice section 979 allows.
#ASSERT (NOT (`ss 979-986 section 979 allows a notice given on the day` (`an offer made on 1 January 2026, open until 30 April 2026, whose acceptance time is not governed by Schedule 1C rules`) (`an offeror with eighty-five per cent by acceptances and a holder who has not accepted`) (Date 1 2 2026)))
-- s 981(6): a notice dated 1 February 2026 has its six weeks end on 15 March 2026; on 14 March section 981(6) has no effect.
#ASSERT (NOT (`ss 979-986 section 981(6) has effect on the day` (Date 1 2 2026) (Date 14 3 2026) FALSE NOTHING))
-- s 981(6): on 15 March it has effect.
#ASSERT `ss 979-986 section 981(6) has effect on the day` (Date 1 2 2026) (Date 15 3 2026) FALSE NOTHING
-- s 986(2): an application pending at the end of the six weeks and not yet disposed of keeps section 981(6) from having effect.
#ASSERT (NOT (`ss 979-986 section 981(6) has effect on the day` (Date 1 2 2026) (Date 20 3 2026) TRUE NOTHING))
-- s 986(2): until the application has been disposed of (here on 10 April), section 981(6) does not have effect.
#ASSERT (NOT (`ss 979-986 section 981(6) has effect on the day` (Date 1 2 2026) (Date 9 4 2026) TRUE (JUST (Date 10 4 2026))))
-- s 986(2): on the day it has been disposed of it has effect.
#ASSERT `ss 979-986 section 981(6) has effect on the day` (Date 1 2 2026) (Date 10 4 2026) TRUE (JUST (Date 10 4 2026))
-- the fixtures: the existing s 983(2) function answers JUST TRUE for holdings of ninety-five per cent and does not for eighty.
#ASSERT (`a holder who may require the offeror to acquire the shares`) EQUALS (JUST TRUE)
#ASSERT (NOT ((`a holder who may not yet require the offeror to acquire the shares`) EQUALS (JUST TRUE)))

§§ `Traces: s 980(2), the offeror's notice and the bar on a late one`

-- s 980(2)(b): the offeror gives notice on 30 June 2026, the last day (day 180 from the offer on 1 January).
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 980(2) the offeror's power to give notice under section 979` (`an offer made on 1 January 2026, open until 30 April 2026, whose acceptance time is not governed by Schedule 1C rules`) (`an offeror with ninety-five per cent by acceptances and a holder who has not accepted`) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 979-986 the offeror` DOES `s 980(2) the offeror gives the holder notice that he desires to acquire the shares` AT 180

-- s 980(2): the offeror gives notice on 1 July 2026, the day after the last day: "No notice may be given ... after the end of".
-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `s 980(2) the offeror's power to give notice under section 979` (`an offer made on 1 January 2026, open until 30 April 2026, whose acceptance time is not governed by Schedule 1C rules`) (`an offeror with ninety-five per cent by acceptances and a holder who has not accepted`) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 979-986 the offeror` DOES `s 980(2) the offeror gives the holder notice that he desires to acquire the shares` AT 181

-- s 980(2)(a) and (3): the offer is governed by Schedule 1C rules, so the three months run to 31 July and a notice on day 200 (19 July) is in time.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 980(2) the offeror's power to give notice under section 979` (`an offer made on 1 January 2026, open until 30 April 2026, whose acceptance time is governed by Schedule 1C rules`) (`an offeror with ninety-five per cent by acceptances and a holder who has not accepted`) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 979-986 the offeror` DOES `s 980(2) the offeror gives the holder notice that he desires to acquire the shares` AT 200

-- s 980(2): no notice given by day 100; the power is still open.
-- EXPECT RESIDUAL
#TRACE `s 980(2) the offeror's power to give notice under section 979` (`an offer made on 1 January 2026, open until 30 April 2026, whose acceptance time is not governed by Schedule 1C rules`) (`an offeror with ninety-five per cent by acceptances and a holder who has not accepted`) AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 100)

-- s 979(2)(a): the offeror holds eighty-five per cent by acceptances, short of ninety, so the power to give notice does not arise.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 980(2) the offeror's power to give notice under section 979` (`an offer made on 1 January 2026, open until 30 April 2026, whose acceptance time is not governed by Schedule 1C rules`) (`an offeror with eighty-five per cent by acceptances and a holder who has not accepted`) AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 100)

§§ `Traces: s 980(4) and (6), the copy of the first notice, the declaration and the offences`

-- s 980(4): the first notice; the copy and the declaration are both sent on the day of the notice.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 980(4) the offeror's duty to send the company a copy of the first notice and a statutory declaration` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 979-986 the offeror` DOES `s 980(4)(a) the offeror sends the company a copy of the notice` AT 0
    PARTY `ss 979-986 the offeror` DOES `s 980(4)(b) the offeror sends the company a statutory declaration in the prescribed form` AT 0

-- s 980(4) and (6)(a): the copy is sent on the day of the notice and the declaration the day after; the offence of failing to send a declaration as required.
-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `s 980(4) the offeror's duty to send the company a copy of the first notice and a statutory declaration` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 979-986 the offeror` DOES `s 980(4)(a) the offeror sends the company a copy of the notice` AT 0
    PARTY `ss 979-986 the offeror` DOES `s 980(4)(b) the offeror sends the company a statutory declaration in the prescribed form` AT 1

-- s 980(4): the notice is not the first the offeror gives in relation to the offer, so the duty does not arise.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 980(4) the offeror's duty to send the company a copy of the first notice and a statutory declaration` FALSE AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 5)

-- s 980(6)(b): the offeror makes a declaration knowing it to be false.
-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `s 980(6)(b) the offeror's duty not to make a false declaration` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 979-986 the offeror` DOES `s 980(6)(b) the offeror makes the declaration knowing it to be false or without reasonable grounds for believing it to be true` AT 3

-- s 980(6)(b): no false declaration; the prohibition stays open.
-- EXPECT RESIDUAL
#TRACE `s 980(6)(b) the offeror's duty not to make a false declaration` AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 10)

§§ `Traces: s 981(3) and s 986(2), the holder's six weeks`

-- s 981(3)(a): the holder indicates a choice on day 30, within six weeks of the notice.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 981(3) the shareholder's six weeks to indicate a choice of consideration` TRUE (Date 1 2 2026) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 979-986 the shareholder` DOES `s 981(3)(a) the shareholder indicates his choice of consideration by a written communication sent to the offeror` AT 30

-- s 981(3)(a): the holder indicates a choice on day 42, the last day of the six weeks.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 981(3) the shareholder's six weeks to indicate a choice of consideration` TRUE (Date 1 2 2026) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 979-986 the shareholder` DOES `s 981(3)(a) the shareholder indicates his choice of consideration by a written communication sent to the offeror` AT 42

-- s 981(3)(a), (b): the holder indicates a choice on day 43, after the six weeks; the choice is out of time, the consideration the notice names applies and nobody is in breach.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 981(3) the shareholder's six weeks to indicate a choice of consideration` TRUE (Date 1 2 2026) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 979-986 the shareholder` DOES `s 981(3)(a) the shareholder indicates his choice of consideration by a written communication sent to the offeror` AT 43

-- s 981(3): the terms of the offer give no choice of consideration, so there is nothing to indicate.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 981(3) the shareholder's six weeks to indicate a choice of consideration` FALSE (Date 1 2 2026) AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 10)

-- s 986(2): the holder applies to the court on day 20, within the six weeks from the notice.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 986(2) the shareholder's six weeks to apply to the court` TRUE (Date 1 2 2026) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 979-986 the shareholder` DOES `s 986(1) the shareholder applies to the court` AT 20

-- s 986(2): the holder applies to the court on day 42, the last day of the six weeks from the notice.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 986(2) the shareholder's six weeks to apply to the court` TRUE (Date 1 2 2026) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 979-986 the shareholder` DOES `s 986(1) the shareholder applies to the court` AT 42

-- s 986(2): the holder applies to the court on day 43, after the six weeks; the application is out of time (the text gives no breach by anyone and no later route).
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 986(2) the shareholder's six weeks to apply to the court` TRUE (Date 1 2 2026) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 979-986 the shareholder` DOES `s 986(1) the shareholder applies to the court` AT 43

-- s 986(1): no notice has been given to the shareholder under section 979, so there is nothing to apply against.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 986(2) the shareholder's six weeks to apply to the court` FALSE (Date 1 2 2026) AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 10)

§§ `Traces: s 981(6), the end of the six weeks`

-- s 981(6): on 15 March 2026, the end of six weeks from the notice of 1 February, the copy is sent and the consideration paid on the same day.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 981(6) the offeror's duty at the end of six weeks` (`an offer made on 1 January 2026, open until 30 April 2026, whose acceptance time is not governed by Schedule 1C rules`) (`an offeror with ninety-five per cent by acceptances and a holder who has not accepted`) (Date 1 2 2026) (Date 15 3 2026) FALSE NOTHING FALSE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 979-986 the offeror` DOES `s 981(6)(a) the offeror sends the company a copy of the notice` AT 0
    PARTY `ss 979-986 the offeror` DOES `s 981(6)(b) the offeror pays or transfers the consideration to the company` AT 0

-- s 981(6): the copy is sent on the day, the consideration is paid the day after: "must immediately".
-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `s 981(6) the offeror's duty at the end of six weeks` (`an offer made on 1 January 2026, open until 30 April 2026, whose acceptance time is not governed by Schedule 1C rules`) (`an offeror with ninety-five per cent by acceptances and a holder who has not accepted`) (Date 1 2 2026) (Date 15 3 2026) FALSE NOTHING FALSE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 979-986 the offeror` DOES `s 981(6)(a) the offeror sends the company a copy of the notice` AT 0
    PARTY `ss 979-986 the offeror` DOES `s 981(6)(b) the offeror pays or transfers the consideration to the company` AT 1

-- s 981(6): 14 March 2026 is a day before the six weeks end, so the duty has not arisen.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 981(6) the offeror's duty at the end of six weeks` (`an offer made on 1 January 2026, open until 30 April 2026, whose acceptance time is not governed by Schedule 1C rules`) (`an offeror with ninety-five per cent by acceptances and a holder who has not accepted`) (Date 1 2 2026) (Date 14 3 2026) FALSE NOTHING FALSE AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 5)

-- s 986(2): an application is pending at the end of the six weeks and has not been disposed of on 20 March; section 981(6) does not have effect.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 981(6) the offeror's duty at the end of six weeks` (`an offer made on 1 January 2026, open until 30 April 2026, whose acceptance time is not governed by Schedule 1C rules`) (`an offeror with ninety-five per cent by acceptances and a holder who has not accepted`) (Date 1 2 2026) (Date 20 3 2026) TRUE NOTHING FALSE AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 5)

-- s 986(2): the application is disposed of on 10 April 2026 and the court has not ordered otherwise; the copy is sent and the consideration paid that day.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 981(6) the offeror's duty at the end of six weeks` (`an offer made on 1 January 2026, open until 30 April 2026, whose acceptance time is not governed by Schedule 1C rules`) (`an offeror with ninety-five per cent by acceptances and a holder who has not accepted`) (Date 1 2 2026) (Date 10 4 2026) TRUE (JUST (Date 10 4 2026)) FALSE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 979-986 the offeror` DOES `s 981(6)(a) the offeror sends the company a copy of the notice` AT 0
    PARTY `ss 979-986 the offeror` DOES `s 981(6)(b) the offeror pays or transfers the consideration to the company` AT 0

-- s 986(1)(a): the court has ordered that the offeror is not entitled and bound to acquire the shares, so section 981(6) leaves no duty.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 981(6) the offeror's duty at the end of six weeks` (`an offer made on 1 January 2026, open until 30 April 2026, whose acceptance time is not governed by Schedule 1C rules`) (`an offeror with ninety-five per cent by acceptances and a holder who has not accepted`) (Date 1 2 2026) (Date 15 3 2026) FALSE NOTHING TRUE AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 5)

-- s 980(2): the notice was given on 1 July 2026, after the last day, so it is not a notice section 979 allows and section 981(6) has no duty to attach to it (1 July plus 42 days is 12 August).
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 981(6) the offeror's duty at the end of six weeks` (`an offer made on 1 January 2026, open until 30 April 2026, whose acceptance time is not governed by Schedule 1C rules`) (`an offeror with ninety-five per cent by acceptances and a holder who has not accepted`) (Date 1 7 2026) (Date 12 8 2026) FALSE NOTHING FALSE AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 5)

§§ `Traces: s 981(9) and s 982, the trust, the separate account and payment into court`

-- s 981(9): the company received the consideration and holds it on trust.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 981(9) the company's duty to hold the consideration on trust` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 979-986 the company` DOES `s 981(9) the company holds the consideration on trust for the person who was entitled to the shares` AT 4

-- s 981(9): the company received nothing under s 981(6)(b), so there is nothing to hold.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 981(9) the company's duty to hold the consideration on trust` FALSE AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 5)

-- s 982(2): the offeror paid money to the company; the company pays it into a separate bank account.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 982(2) the company's duty to pay into a separate bank account` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 979-986 the company` DOES `s 982(2) the company pays the money, and any dividend or other sum accruing, into a separate bank account that complies with subsection (3)` AT 3

-- s 982(2): the offeror paid nothing under s 981(6), so section 982 does not apply.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 982(2) the company's duty to pay into a separate bank account` FALSE AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 5)

-- s 982(4) and (5): the person cannot be found, enquiries were made, twelve years have elapsed since 1 January 2014 on 2 January 2026; the company pays into court on day 5.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 982(4) the company's duty to pay the consideration into court` TRUE TRUE (Date 1 1 2014) (Date 2 1 2026) FALSE `England and Wales` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 979-986 the company` DOES `s 982(4) the company pays the consideration into court` AT 5

-- s 982(4): the same facts and no payment by day 400; the Act gives no time, so the duty stays open.
-- EXPECT RESIDUAL
#TRACE `s 982(4) the company's duty to pay the consideration into court` TRUE TRUE (Date 1 1 2014) (Date 2 1 2026) FALSE `England and Wales` AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 400)

-- s 982(5)(b): only eleven years have elapsed (1 June 2025) and the company is not wound up, so subsection (5) does not apply.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 982(4) the company's duty to pay the consideration into court` TRUE TRUE (Date 1 1 2014) (Date 1 6 2025) FALSE `England and Wales` AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 5)

§§ `Traces: s 983 and s 984(2), the holder's right to require acquisition and its three months`

-- s 984(2)(a): no notice under s 984(3) yet; the holder requires the offeror to acquire on day 91 (30 July 2026), the last day, and the offeror acquires on day 95.
