-- s 984(2)(b): the notice under s 984(3) is dated 30 May 2026, later than the end of the acceptance period, so the three months run to 30 August (day 122); the holder requires on day 110 and the offeror acquires on day 115.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 984(2) the shareholder's three months to require the offeror to acquire the shares` (`a holder who may require the offeror to acquire the shares`) (Date 30 4 2026) (JUST (Date 30 5 2026)) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 979-986 the shareholder` DOES `s 983 the shareholder requires the offeror to acquire the shares by a written communication` AT 110
    PARTY `ss 979-986 the offeror` DOES `s 985(2) the offeror acquires the shares on the terms of the offer or on such other terms as may be agreed` AT 115

-- s 983(2)(b): the offeror's holdings stop at eighty per cent, so the holder has no right to require and no window opens.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 984(2) the shareholder's three months to require the offeror to acquire the shares` (`a holder who may not yet require the offeror to acquire the shares`) (Date 30 4 2026) NOTHING AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 10)

§§ `Traces: s 984(3) to (5), the offeror's notice of the rights and the offences`

-- s 984(3): the offeror gives the notice of the rights on day 10, well within the month.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 984(3) the offeror's duty to give the shareholder notice of his rights` (`a holder who may require the offeror to acquire the shares`) FALSE (Date 30 4 2026) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 979-986 the offeror` DOES `s 984(3) the offeror gives the shareholder notice of the rights and the period` AT 10

-- s 984(3): the holder has the right, the offeror has given no s 979 notice, and the offeror gives the notice of the rights on day 30 (30 May 2026), the last day of the month.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 984(3) the offeror's duty to give the shareholder notice of his rights` (`a holder who may require the offeror to acquire the shares`) FALSE (Date 30 4 2026) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 979-986 the offeror` DOES `s 984(3) the offeror gives the shareholder notice of the rights and the period` AT 30

-- s 984(3): the offeror gives the notice on day 31, the day after the month; the offence of s 984(5).
-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `s 984(3) the offeror's duty to give the shareholder notice of his rights` (`a holder who may require the offeror to acquire the shares`) FALSE (Date 30 4 2026) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 979-986 the offeror` DOES `s 984(3) the offeror gives the shareholder notice of the rights and the period` AT 31

-- s 984(3): no notice by day 15; the month is still running.
-- EXPECT RESIDUAL
#TRACE `s 984(3) the offeror's duty to give the shareholder notice of his rights` (`a holder who may require the offeror to acquire the shares`) FALSE (Date 30 4 2026) AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 15)

-- s 984(4): the offeror has given the shareholder a notice under section 979 in respect of the shares, so subsection (3) does not apply.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 984(3) the offeror's duty to give the shareholder notice of his rights` (`a holder who may require the offeror to acquire the shares`) TRUE (Date 30 4 2026) AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 40)

-- s 983(2)(b): the holder has no right to require, so the offeror owes no notice of it.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 984(3) the offeror's duty to give the shareholder notice of his rights` (`a holder who may not yet require the offeror to acquire the shares`) FALSE (Date 30 4 2026) AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 40)

-- s 984(5): the offeror is a company, fails to comply with s 984(3), and an officer is in default; the officer commits the offence.
-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `s 984(5) the officer's duty not to be in default in the offeror company's failure` TRUE TRUE (JUST TRUE) FALSE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 979-986 an officer of the offeror company who is in default` DOES `s 984(5) the officer is in default in the offeror company's failure, or the failure is attributable to the officer's neglect` AT 3

-- s 984(5): the same facts, and the prohibition stays open until the default or neglect is shown.
-- EXPECT RESIDUAL
#TRACE `s 984(5) the officer's duty not to be in default in the offeror company's failure` TRUE TRUE (JUST TRUE) FALSE AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 10)

-- s 984(5): the offeror is not a company, so the second sentence does not apply to any officer.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 984(5) the officer's duty not to be in default in the offeror company's failure` TRUE FALSE (JUST TRUE) FALSE AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 10)

